# Provenance of the committed native cores

WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. `SHA256SUMS` proves the two copies of each library match each
other. It says nothing about whether they match the SOURCE — and they did not: the cores
shipped in this tree were built from the 0.7.12 source while `qeli/src` had moved on, so
the GUI clients silently carried an older realtls/FFI core than the repository described.
Nothing in review or CI could have caught that. This file records what the current
binaries were actually built from, so the question has an answer.

source-digest : 0dfac80b50d2bdd1964817dee8ac87f7311cde63bf61efade7a40abd7e32b635
base-commit   : e0ce217b630d9dfd7db5f59936bb41e6d68eb69d
dirty-sources : 0 file(s) modified vs base-commit at build time
built-on      : lab .10 (Windows/macOS), lab .11 (Android); isolated A/B jobs, 2026-10-13
toolchain     : pinned inventories in native-libs/reproducibility/{desktop,android}.json
panic         : CARGO_PROFILE_RELEASE_PANIC=unwind  (REQUIRED — the catch_unwind guards in
                protocol/realtls/{ffi,jni}.rs are inert under panic=abort)
targets       : x86_64-pc-windows-gnu · universal2-apple-darwin ·
                aarch64-linux-android · x86_64-linux-android

`source-digest` is SHA256 over `"<path> <sha256>
"` for every `qeli/src/**/*.rs`,
`qeli/Cargo.toml`, `qeli/Cargo.lock`, `qeli/.cargo/config.toml` and the executable
native recipes listed in `scripts/native_repro.py` (`BUILD_INPUTS`), paths sorted.
Recompute it with
`python native-libs/provenance.py --check`: a mismatch means the cores are stale relative
to the source in this tree and must be rebuilt before release.
